sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as HTTP Client
    participant Controller as Controller Layer<br/>(HTTP REST)
    participant Service as Service Layer<br/>(gRPC Server)
    participant Repository as Repository Layer<br/>(gRPC Server)
    participant Cache as Redis Cache
    participant DB as MySQL Database

    Note over Client,Controller: External Communication<br/>JSON over HTTP REST

    Client->>Controller: POST /api/auth/login<br/>{"username": "user", "password": "pass"}
    activate Controller

    Note over Controller,Service: Internal Communication<br/>Protocol Buffers over gRPC<br/>⚡ 2.78x faster

    Controller->>Service: AuthenticateUser(username, password)<br/>via gRPC (port 50051)
    activate Service

    Service->>Service: Validate Credentials<br/>Apply Business Rules

    Service->>Repository: GetUserByUsername(username)<br/>via gRPC (port 50052)
    activate Repository

    Repository->>Cache: Check Cache<br/>GET user:username
    activate Cache
    Cache-->>Repository: Cache Miss
    deactivate Cache

    Repository->>DB: SELECT * FROM users<br/>WHERE username = ?
    activate DB
    DB-->>Repository: User Record
    deactivate DB

    Repository->>Cache: Store in Cache<br/>SET user:username
    activate Cache
    Cache-->>Repository: Cached
    deactivate Cache

    Repository-->>Service: UserResponse<br/>(Protocol Buffer)<br/>⚡ ~1.5ms vs ~9.5ms HTTP
    deactivate Repository

    Service->>Service: Generate JWT Tokens<br/>(Access + Refresh)

    Service-->>Controller: AuthResponse<br/>(Protocol Buffer)<br/>⚡ 6.30x faster for point queries
    deactivate Service

    Controller->>Controller: Serialize to JSON

    Controller-->>Client: 200 OK<br/>{"access_token": "jwt...", "refresh_token": "jwt..."}
    deactivate Controller

    Note over Controller,Repository: Performance Benefits:<br/>• Binary Protocol (smaller payload)<br/>• HTTP/2 Multiplexing<br/>• Persistent Connections<br/>• Type Safety (Protocol Buffers)
